      {
        "block_id": "doc_e57ded6cc07f6574:s4_platform_versions:b1",
        "source_id": "aws-fargate",
        "chunk_id": "doc_e57ded6cc07f6574:s4_platform_versions:b1",
        "heading": null,
        "text": "Context: Architect for AWS Fargate for Amazon ECS Heading: Platform versions Function: explanation Text: New revisions of platform versions are released as the runtime environment evolves, for example, if there are kernel or operating system updates, new features, bug fixes, or security updates. A Fargate platform version is updated by making a new platform version revision. Each task runs on one platform version revision during its lifecycle. If you want to use the latest platform version revision, then you must start a new task. A new task that runs on Fargate always runs on the latest revision of a platform version, ensuring that tasks are always started on secure and patched infrastructure.",
